#: ../../build123d/docs/selectors.rst:56
msgid ""
"The operand types are: Axis, Plane, SortBy, GeomType, and Convexity. An Axis"
" is a base object with an origin and a direction with several predefined "
"values such as ``Axis.X``, ``Axis.Y``, and ``Axis.Z``; however, any Axis "
"could be used as an operand (e.g. ``Axis((1,2,3),(0.5,0,-0.5))`` is valid) -"
" see :class:`~geometry.Axis` for a complete description. A Plane is a "
"coordinate system defined by an origin, x_dir (X direction), y_dir (Y "
"direction), and z_dir (Z direction). See :class:`~geometry.Plane` for a "
"complete description. Filtering by a Plane will return faces/edges parallel "
"to it. SortBy, GeomType and Convexity are python Enum class described here:"
msgstr ""

